course: dictionary
lesson: 8959
title: Simple: easy, plain or basic
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word simple has more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «Test the simple causes first: is the socket switched on, is the cable in?» Here simple means easy to check and basic, the first and most obvious things to look at.
explain: Simple can also mean plain, with nothing extra added. «Resting from the ego can be as simple as breathing slowly and being present.» Here simple means easy to do, with no special skill needed. Ask yourself: is the writer saying something is easy, plain, or basic?
explain: In «a simple dice game», simple means it has few rules and is easy to learn. Compare that with chess, which has many rules and takes much more thinking. Simple is the opposite of complicated.
fact: Simple means easy to understand or do, not complicated.
fact: Simple can mean plain, without decoration or extra things, as in «a simple dress».
fact: Simple can mean basic and made of few parts, as in simple machines.
fact: In maths, to simplify a fraction means to make it simpler: 4/8 becomes 1/2.
fact: Simple machines are basic tools in science: the lever, pulley, wheel and axle, and ramp.
exercise: In «test the simple causes first», what does simple mean? | Painted in bright colours | Hard to find and very rare | *Basic and easy to check | Made of many parts
exercise: «Some games are won by thinking and some by luck (a simple dice game).» What does simple suggest about the dice game? | *Easy to play, with few rules | Played only with a computer | Very long, with many hard rules | Based on a lot of maths
exercise: «Mum wore a simple dress with no lace or sparkles.» What does simple mean here? | Dirty and torn | *Plain, with no decoration | Very expensive | Covered in sequins
test: Simplify the fraction 4/8. What is the answer? | 1/4 | 2/8 | 4/4 | *1/2
test: Which of these is a simple machine? | Computer | *Ramp | Car engine | Television
exam: Which word means the opposite of simple, as in «not easy to understand»? | Plain | Easy | Basic | *Complicated
